From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350-b2q: enable the QUP2 GPI DMA controller

spi14 (QUP2 SE0, the bus stock gives the eSE) is enabled, but its serial
engine runs in GPI mode and gpi_dma2 was left disabled. geni_spi then
deferred forever ("Failed to get tx DMA ch"), and as a consumer of gcc and
rpmhpd it kept both from ever reaching sync_state(). Enable gpi_dma2.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts |    9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts
index eb3d6cd..e1d0ec6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts
@@ -1620,6 +1620,15 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * QUP2's GPI DMA. SE14 (spi14, the eSE bus stock gives to HLOS) runs in GPI
+ * mode: without this controller its driver defers forever ("Failed to get
+ * tx DMA ch"), and with it gcc and rpmhpd never reach sync_state.
+ */
+&gpi_dma2 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 // GPU and MDSS (displays)
 &gpu {
 	status = "okay";
